{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew","id":1561587,"title":"Aberrant: The Eruption - My V20 Compatable Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-10T21:48:27-07:00","id":1561587,"title":"Aberrant: The Eruption - My V20 Compatable Homebrew","content":"I'm a big fan of the Aberrant setting and the superhero genre in general, as well as other White Wolf/Onyx Path games like the classic Wolrd of Darkness, and I wanted to make a version of Aberrant that was rules-compatable with the 20th Anniversary Editions of the World of Darkness games so I could in include paranormal plots and characters in my Aberrant games. Way I see it, The Avengers need characters like Dr. Strange and Thor running around, y'know? I also rebuilt the power system from the ground up, making it a little more streamlined and balanced and a lot more flexible. I thought I would share it here, see what some other Aberrant/WoD fans think:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yiLu_zTatBWFvsWW1xPLlzdRu3LXmp54yav6BFqw8RY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yiLu_zTatBWFvsWW1xPLlzdRu3LXmp54yav6BFqw8RY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yiLu_zTatBWFvsWW1xPLlzdRu3LXmp54yav6BFqw8RY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yiLu_zTatBWFvsWW1xPLlzdRu3LXmp54yav6BFqw8RY/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also, fair warning, this contains my notes for the game I run, and I took some liberties with the lore and changed a few things, so don't be surprised if you see the stats for canonically dead characters or characters from other franchises transplanted into Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T22:55:52-07:00","id":1561588,"title":"","content":"Interesting decision to have Mercer be a Nova as well, albeit still with his time control powers. I'm assuming its to simplify things further considering how big the World is already?<br /> <br /> For the Eufiber background, I think the values given are a bit high for the lower dots. It's effectively the Armor power but for free, and outweighs the power of conventional armor at the lower end. I think a less bottom-heavy version of the statline could be 1/2/3/5/8, which still gives a high bonus at maximum investment while not invalidating the Armor power as a whole.<br /> <br /> From what I've seen looking through here, Dormancy is no longer a thing? On the one hand, that is a way to make Aberrations more important in the day-to-day lives of the characters, though it does make secret identities a lot harder to pull off.<br /> <br /> I'd need to do a more in-depth review later, this is just my thoughts after giving things a quick skim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T06:40:24-07:00","id":1561599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1561588#post1561588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting decision to have Mercer be a Nova as well, albeit still with his time control powers. I'm assuming its to simplify things further considering how big the World is already?</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. The whole &quot;he's not a Nova or a Psychic but a third thing that seems the same as a Nova&quot; is just an extrenuous detail, IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1561588#post1561588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Eufiber background, I think the values given are a bit high for the lower dots. It's effectively the Armor power but for free, and outweighs the power of conventional armor at the lower end. I think a less bottom-heavy version of the statline could be 1/2/3/5/8, which still gives a high bonus at maximum investment while not invalidating the Armor power as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad idea, that's worth considering.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1561588#post1561588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've seen looking through here, Dormancy is no longer a thing? On the one hand, that is a way to make Aberrations more important in the day-to-day lives of the characters, though it does make secret identities a lot harder to pull off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just never really cared for Dormancy as a mechanic. Like you said, it makes Aberrations a bigger deal, which feels important to me. I could be convinced to put it back in with a strong enough argument, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T06:58:46-07:00","id":1561603,"title":"","content":"Oh, also, I comissioned a custom character sheet for Aberrant: The Erruption from Mr. Gone:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Aberrant/Aberrant_TheErruption_4-Page_OWoD_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Aberrant/Aberrant_TheErruption_4-Page_OWoD_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Aberrant/Aberrant_TheErruption_4-Page_OWoD_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Aberrant/Aberrant_TheErruption_4-Page_OWoD_Interactive.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T14:41:34-07:00","id":1562133,"title":"","content":"I have been making active edits, changed, and additions, if anyone wants to check them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T15:39:37-07:00","id":1562239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1561588#post1561588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting decision to have Mercer be a Nova as well, albeit still with his time control powers. I'm assuming its to simplify things further considering how big the World is already?<br /> <br /> For the Eufiber background, I think the values given are a bit high for the lower dots. It's effectively the Armor power but for free, and outweighs the power of conventional armor at the lower end. I think a less bottom-heavy version of the statline could be 1/2/3/5/8, which still gives a high bonus at maximum investment while not invalidating the Armor power as a whole.<br /> <br /> From what I've seen looking through here, Dormancy is no longer a thing? On the one hand, that is a way to make Aberrations more important in the day-to-day lives of the characters, though it does make secret identities a lot harder to pull off.<br /> <br /> I'd need to do a more in-depth review later, this is just my thoughts after giving things a quick skim.</div> </div> </div> </div>I decided to take your advice and add Dormancy back in. I'm keeping Euphiber as-is, though, and just giving it the property of stacking with other types of armor. That's a lot of protection, but then this is Aberrant we're talking about, people hit hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T13:09:37-07:00","id":1563370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1561603#post1561603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, also, I comissioned a custom character sheet for Aberrant: The Erruption from Mr. Gone:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Aberrant/Aberrant_TheErruption_4-Page_OWoD_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/p...nteractive.pdf</a></div> </div> </div> </div>A little late in seeing this, but thanks for posting the link! Glad I could help! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-30T12:31:52-07:00","id":1564434,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone, just bumping this to mention that I added the &quot;Taint&quot; mechanic back into this version of the game, though I changed the name to &quot;Contamination&quot; in order to avoid the juvenile connotations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-02T09:07:54-07:00","id":1564485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1564434#post1564434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey everyone, just bumping this to mention that I added the &quot;Taint&quot; mechanic back into this version of the game, though I changed the name to &quot;Contamination&quot; in order to avoid the juvenile connotations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mr. Gone was kind enough to make a new version of the character sheet with the &quot;Contamination&quot; Trait added:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Aberrant/Aberrant_TheErruption_v2_4-Page_OWoD_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Aberrant/Aberrant_TheErruption_v2_4-Page_OWoD_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Aberrant/Aberrant_TheErruption_v2_4-Page_OWoD_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/Aberrant/Aberrant_TheErruption_v2_4-Page_OWoD_Interactive.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T14:19:24-07:00","id":1564572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Question</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1561599#post1561599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Precisely. The whole &quot;he's not a Nova or a Psychic but a third thing that seems the same as a Nova&quot; is just an extrenuous detail, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. If you're going to say that psychics aren't Novas, I see no reason not to say that paramorphs also aren't. But you do you. <br /> <br /> Personally, I would juxtapose Novas against Mages rather than Kindred, by doing something similar to an old Pyramid article I once saw: \u201cTo Tear the Scales From Their Eyes\u201d. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T16:00:50-07:00","id":1564574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1564572#post1564572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. If you're going to say that psychics aren't Novas, I see no reason not to say that paramorphs also aren't. But you do you.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would juxtapose Novas against Mages rather than Kindred, by doing something similar to an old Pyramid article I once saw: \u201cTo Tear the Scales From Their Eyes\u201d.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I juxtapose them against the entire World of Darkness. There's a section in my doc called &quot;A World of Darkness&quot; which goes over how each of the main game lines react to Novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T16:02:17-07:00","id":1564575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1564572#post1564572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. If you're going to say that psychics aren't Novas, I see no reason not to say that paramorphs also aren't. But you do you.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would juxtapose Novas against Mages rather than Kindred, by doing something similar to an old Pyramid article I once saw: \u201cTo Tear the Scales From Their Eyes\u201d.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, also, what Pyramid article? Could you elaborate on that, I'm curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T04:34:38-07:00","id":1564606,"title":"","content":"The premise was that a group of mages deliberately sacrificed themselves in a massive Paradox-inducing Working to make it blatantly obvious to the public that Magick is real. The result was the Galatea Event and the emergence of Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T11:31:55-07:00","id":1564612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1564606#post1564606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise was that a group of mages deliberately sacrificed themselves in a massive Paradox-inducing Working to make it blatantly obvious to the public that Magick is real. The result was the Galatea Event and the emergence of Novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fun idea. I wonder how Divis Mal would feel about being the puppet of some wizards' spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T10:27:13-07:00","id":1564643,"title":"","content":"To be fair, my own take on it would be to go back to the Adventure! era, and replace or predate the Hammersmith Event (1922) with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Czar_Vargo\" target=\"_blank\">Czar Vargo's attempted conquest of the world</a> (1914): if you predate it, Vargo becomes the motivation for Hammersmith's work; if you replace it, the Backlash from Vargo's stunt floods the world in Telluric Energy. In the latter case, I'd adjust the date of Vargo's stunt to take place in 1922, and I'd arrange it so that Max Mercer, Michael Donighal, and Sara Kaur are somehow directly involved in the incident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-10T15:08:11-07:00","id":1564672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1564643#post1564643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, my own take on it would be to go back to the Adventure! era, and replace or predate the Hammersmith Event (1922) with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Czar_Vargo\" target=\"_blank\">Czar Vargo's attempted conquest of the world</a> (1914): if you predate it, Vargo becomes the motivation for Hammersmith's work; if you replace it, the Backlash from Vargo's stunt floods the world in Telluric Energy. In the latter case, I'd adjust the date of Vargo's stunt to take place in 1922, and I'd arrange it so that Max Mercer, Michael Donighal, and Sara Kaur are somehow directly involved in the incident.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with Czar Vargo's stunt predating the Hammersmith Event. Timeline-wise, it just kind of works out. Maybe Hammersmith was a Mage and one of the few people to remember what Czar Vargo did, and invented his machine as a precaution against future such crisis events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2403-the-question","name":"The Question","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-11T13:10:20-07:00","id":1564693,"title":"","content":"It also depends on how much of the Trinity Continuum you want to incorporate. TC:Aether is set in the time frame of Victorian Mage, before the nascent Technocratic Union reorganized and the Electrodyne Engineers jumped ship to become the Sons of Ether. What happens if <i>that's </i>the divergence point? TC:Aether is the result of an intrusion into the timeline by cross-time invaders (referred to as the Martians), with the appearance of Aether as a byproduct of said invasion. If those Martians had invaded the world of Victorian Mage, what would have happened?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-12T15:37:39-07:00","id":1564712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1561587-aberrant-the-eruption-my-v20-compatable-homebrew?p=1564693#post1564693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also depends on how much of the Trinity Continuum you want to incorporate. TC:Aether is set in the time frame of Victorian Mage, before the nascent Technocratic Union reorganized and the Electrodyne Engineers jumped ship to become the Sons of Ether. What happens if <i>that's </i>the divergence point? TC:Aether is the result of an intrusion into the timeline by cross-time invaders (referred to as the Martians), with the appearance of Aether as a byproduct of said invasion. If those Martians had invaded the world of Victorian Mage, what would have happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>As of right now, I'm only working with the original three TC settings and incorporating the World of Darkness into them. I am especially focused on the role that the supernatural can play in the world of Aberrant.","signature":"","edited"